  "funFacts": [
    {
      "title": "Mostar means the bridge keeper",
      "body": "The city’s name links to most — bridge — and the people who kept the crossing. Stari Most is the postcard; the whole old town is the story."
    },
    {
      "title": "Ovdje vs tamo",
      "body": "Bosnian learners often mix here and there. Pair each word with a hand gesture: palm down for ovdje, point away for tamo."
    },
    {
      "title": "Kod + name",
      "body": "Kod Amire is how you say you are at Amira’s place. You will use kod + a person constantly for homes, shops, and cafés."
    },
    {
      "title": "Spoiler, softly",
      "body": "Book 1 saves the real Mostar trip for later. Lesson 5 only plants the map pin — and Emir’s grin."
    }
  ],
